<title>USA: Perkin-Elmer sues TA Instruments over patent.</title>
<headline>Perkin-Elmer sues TA Instruments over patent.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Del. 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Perkin-Elmer Corp of Norwalk, Conn., alleges in a lawsuit that its patent for &quot;Apparatus and method for differential analysis using real and imaginary signal components&quot; is being infringed by products made by TA Instruments Inc.</p>
<p>In papers filed last week, Perkin-Elmer asked the U.S. District Court in Delaware to enjoin TA from infringement and for an award of unspecified damages.</p>
<p>Officials of TA Instruments, of New Castle, Del., could not be reached for comment.</p>
</text>
